  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 4, 5) despite positive sentiment spikes; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 10-20 EUR.",
    "Forecasts display significant lag in reacting to sudden price spikes (e.g., 76.67 in Ex 4/5); the model predicts a slow linear recovery while actual prices peak sharply and then revert.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (positive spikes amidst negative trends), the model ignores the volatility context and assumes monotonic growth, leading to systematic overestimation.",
    "Mean reversion is underestimated; true outcomes frequently drop below the forecasted trend line within 5-10 days after a spike, whereas the model projects continued ascent.",
    "Horizon-specific error: The 30-day forecast fails to capture intra-period volatility, resulting in a smooth curve that misses both the peak magnitude and the subsequent correction phase."
  ]
